# Ruff cache
.ruff_cache/

# Local working files, kept on disk but out of git.
#   test_data/ — raw QuantStudio plate exports for real studies. Nothing in the
#     suite reads them (the tests build their own frames), so they are input for
#     manual checks, not fixtures.
#   docs/ — local write-ups. This ignores the WHOLE tree, so a doc that is meant
#     to be tracked needs an explicit `git add -f`.
#   효능평가항목_update.xlsx — the in-vitro assay ledger. Its 21 rows were already
#     reconciled into EFFICACY_CONFIG on 2026-07-31; where the two disagree the
#     code deliberately wins (see the 탄력 and 장벽 comments in
#     qpcr/constants.py). Named explicitly rather than ignoring *.xlsx, because
#     a workbook IS tracked (qPCR_진정_20260205_1424.xlsx) and a blanket rule
#     would quietly hide any future intentional one.
# The previous entry here read "# test data/" with a space and never matched the
# real directory name.
docs/
test_data/
효능평가항목_update.xlsx

# Tool state (Claude Code / Playwright / Superpowers)
.claude/
.playwright-mcp/
.superpowers/

# QA / audit screenshots (transient debugging artifacts, not source-of-truth)
audit_*.png
qa_*.png
test_*.png
app-running.png
upload-state.png
